** Warping and shear deformations of a rectangular beam section (WARP2D8),
** with the stresses due to Vz, Vy, Mxp and Mxs, see Kindmann & Kraus, figure 7.7.
*material, name=linearelastic, id=steel, provider=edelweiss
210000.0, 0.3

*section, name=sec1, thickness=1.0, material=steel, type=plane
all

*job, name=beamSection, domain=2d
*solver, solver=BeamSection, name=theSectionSolver

*modelGenerator, generator=planeRectQuad, name=gen
x0=-50, l=100.0, y0=-100, h=200.0, elType=WARP2D8, elProvider=edelweiss, nX=4, nY=8

*fieldOutput
>>perNode, elSet=all, field=warping, result=U, name=warping
>>perNode, elSet=all, field=shear deformation, result=U, name=shearDeformation
>>perElement, elSet=all, result=shear stress, name=shearStress, quadraturePoint=0, f(x)=x

*step, solver=theSectionSolver
maxInc=1.0
>>sectionforces, name=forces, Vy=5e4, Vz=1e5, Mxp=1e6, Mxs=2e6
